# Techno Sapiens Section Development

Authoritative boilerplate for section PHP, partials, SCSS, ACF, and assets. Use with [060-create-section.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/060-create-section.mdc). Copy `sections/section-content`. Do not generate column-based `blocks/` classes.

Placeholders: `[section-slug]` = kebab-case with `section-` prefix (`section-content`). `[SectionName]` = PascalCase (`SectionContent`). `[section_slug]` = slug with underscores (`section_content`).

## File location

✅ `/public/wp-content/themes/technosapiens/sections/[section-slug]/`  
❌ `/blocks/[section-slug]/`

## PHP class (`[SectionName].php`)

Keep the class thin. Registration, enqueue, ACF save, and render live in `SectionReferenceTrait`.

```php
<?php

namespace TechnoSapiens;

use TechnoSapiens\Core\Singleton;

class SectionContent extends Singleton {
    use SectionReferenceTrait;

    public const SECTION_ID = 'section_section_content';
    public const SECTION_SLUG = 'section-content';

    protected function __construct() {
        $supports = [];
        $postTypes = [];

        $this->registerReferenceSection(
            __('Content section.', Theme::TEXT_DOMAIN),
            'text',
            false,
            $supports,
            $postTypes
        );
    }

    public static function getSectionLabel(): string {
        return __('Content', Theme::TEXT_DOMAIN);
    }
}
```

### Constants

| Constant | Example | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `SECTION_ID` | `section_section_content` | ACF `name` (`section_` + `[section_slug]`) |
| `SECTION_SLUG` | `section-content` | Folder, `has_block('acf/section-' . slug)`, assets, ACF location suffix |

### `registerReferenceSection($description, $icon, $hasScript, $supports, $postTypes, $blockMode)`

The trait registers an ACF **block v3** section (`api_version` / `acf_block_version` 3). Do not set `mode` to `edit`. Default mode is `preview`. Pass `$hasScript = true` only when `js/[section-slug].js` exists.

Supports default: `customClassName` false, `align` false, `mode` false, `reusable` true.

### What the trait already does (do not duplicate)

* `acf_register_block_type` with `name` => `SECTION_ID`
* Frontend enqueue when `has_block('acf/section-' . SECTION_SLUG)` on `$post` / `$otherPosts`
* Editor enqueue via `enqueue_block_assets` when `is_admin()`
* CSS key: `SECTION_SLUG . '-style.css'`
* JS key (if `$hasScript`): `SECTION_SLUG . '-script.js'`
* ACF JSON save into `sections/SECTION_SLUG/acf-json/` as `SECTION_SLUG.json` (matched by field group **key**, not title)
* `render()` via `Partial::render` from `sections/SECTION_SLUG/partials/`
* Optional inserter preview image: `preview/SECTION_SLUG.jpg`

ACF JSON **load** paths are registered in `Theme::registerSectionAcfJsonLoadPaths()`.

## Partial (`partials/[section-slug].php`)

`get_field()` without `$post_id`. Collect data at the top. Alternative PHP syntax (`:`, `endif`).

Required outer pattern (from `section-content`):

```php
<?php

use TechnoSapiens\Core\Formatting;
use TechnoSapiens\Core\Image;
use TechnoSapiens\SectionMargins;
use TechnoSapiens\SectionReferencePartial;

$contentType = get_field('content_type') ?? '';
$containerClasses = SectionReferencePartial::getContainerClasses('section-content');
$marginTop = SectionMargins::getMarginTop();
$marginBottom = SectionMargins::getMarginBottom();
?>

<?php if ($hasContent) : ?>
    <div class="<?php echo esc_attr(implode(' ', $containerClasses)); ?>"<?php if ($marginTop) : ?> data-mt="<?php echo esc_attr($marginTop); ?>"<?php endif; ?><?php if ($marginBottom) : ?> data-mb="<?php echo esc_attr($marginBottom); ?>"<?php endif; ?>>
        <div class="container container--narrow section-content__container">
            <!-- BEM content -->
        </div>
    </div>
<?php endif; ?>
```

* `getContainerClasses()` always includes `section` and the slug. Optional ACF `bg` adds `[slug]--bg-*` and `ts-has-dark-background`.
* Margins come from shared fields `section_margin_top` / `section_margin_bottom` (`SectionMargins`). Do not add those fields to the section JSON.
* Do not use legacy block wrappers, `VisualMarginComponent`, or `PreviewNotificationComponent` unless an existing section already does.

WYSIWYG: `Formatting::toHtml($html)`. Buttons: `ts-button` + style/color modifiers and `ts-button__text` (see `section-page-buttons`).

Images (array return format, as in `section-content`):

```php
$contentImage = get_field('content_image') ?? [];
$contentImageId = !empty($contentImage['ID']) ? (int) $contentImage['ID'] : 0;

echo Image::render([
    'blockClass' => 'section-content',
    'sources' => [
        [
            'id' => $contentImageId,
            'size' => 'full',
        ],
    ],
]);
```

## SCSS

`scss/[section-slug].scss` only unless editor CSS is required. Webpack entry becomes `[section-slug]-style.css`.

```scss
@use "../../../scss/util/util-mixins" as mixins;
@use "../../../scss/util/util-variables" as vars;

.section-content {
    $self: &;

    &__text {
        gap: calc(var(--ts-gutter-width, 1rem) / 2);

        &--bg-white {
            background-color: var(--ts-color-white, white);

            @include mixins.mq-up(lg) {
                padding: 3rem;
            }
        }
    }
}
```

Nest breakpoints inside elements. Prefer `mq-up`. `mq-down` is allowed when the design needs it.

## JS (optional)

Omit the file and keep `$hasScript` false when native HTML/CSS is enough (accordion uses `<details>`). If JS is required: `js/[section-slug].js`, `$hasScript = true`, follow [040-javascript-organization.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/040-javascript-organization.mdc).

## ACF JSON (`acf-json/[section-slug].json`)

* Filename equals `SECTION_SLUG` (`section-content.json`).
* Title: English, e.g. `"Section - Content"`. All labels, choices, and button texts in English.
* Field `name`: snake_case (`content_type`). That is what `get_field()` uses.
* `location.value`: `acf\/section-section-content` (`acf/section-` + `SECTION_SLUG`).
* Do **not** include margin fields.
* Keep keys unique. Saves are matched by group `key` in the JSON file.

After creating a section, add the same location to `acf-json/section-settings.json` so shared margins appear in the editor.

## Register in `functions.php`

```php
public static function initBlocks(): void {
    SectionAccordion::getInstance();
    SectionCtaBanner::getInstance();
    SectionPageButtons::getInstance();
    SectionContent::getInstance();
    SectionUsps::getInstance();
    SectionStats::getInstance();
    SectionDivider::getInstance();
    // [SectionName]::getInstance();
}
```

Classes autoload from `sections/`. No extra imports.

## Checklist

- Thin class + `SectionReferenceTrait`
- `SECTION_ID` / `SECTION_SLUG` as in `section-content`
- Partial: `getContainerClasses` + `SectionMargins` + standard `section` class
- SCSS `@use` mixins/vars and `--ts-` variables
- ACF location `acf/section-[section-slug]`
- `section-settings.json` location added
- `initBlocks()` updated
- No `BlockMarginComponent`, no legacy block wrappers, no `blocks/` path
